\DOC SAFE_UNIFY_REFL_TAC

\TYPE {SAFE_UNIFY_REFL_TAC : term list ref -> string list ref -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes an equational goal {A ?- t = u} whose right-hand side is a variable (or
a term headed by a permitted symbol) by instantiating it against the left-hand
side, leaving no subgoals.

\DESCRIBE
The first argument, {allowed_vars_ref : term list ref}, is a reference to the
list of variables that may be instantiated; in the observed traces it holds
either a designated variable list or an empty one. The second,
{allowed_var_prefixes_ref : string list ref}, is a reference to a list of name
prefixes whose matching symbols are additionally permitted during the
unification. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is a single equation between
two terms of the same type, the tactic discharges it completely:
{
       A ?- t = u
       ==========  SAFE_UNIFY_REFL_TAC allowed_vars_ref allowed_var_prefixes_ref
}
{
   
}
\noindent In the observed traces the right-hand side {u} is either a plain
variable or an application of a symbol whose name matches the allowed-prefix
list, and the left-hand side {t} is a concrete term built from the state
recorded in the assumptions {A}, which are left untouched.

\COMMENTS
All observed applications close the goal, so no other outcome is demonstrated.

\ENDDOC
